{"name":"Santorini","hex":"#41b0d0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Santorini","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island in the Cyclades, Greece."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Santorini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santorini","blocks":[{"text":"Santorini, officially Thira or Thera, is a Greek island in the southern Aegean Sea, about 200 km (120 mi) southeast from the mainland. It is the largest island of a small, circular archipelago formed by the Santorini caldera. It is the southernmost member of the Cyclades group of islands, with an area of approximately 73 km2 (28 mi2) and a 2021 census population of 15,480. The municipality of Santorini includes the inhabited islands of Santorini and Therasia, and the uninhabited islands of Nea Kameni, Palaia Kameni, Aspronisi, Anydros, and Christiana. The total land area is 90 km2 (35 mi2). Santorini is part of the Thira regional unit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2011_Dimos_Thiras.png/330px-2011_Dimos_Thiras.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santorini"},{"title":"Santorini (wine)","blocks":[{"text":"Santorini is a Greek wine region located on the archipelago of Santorini in the southern Cyclades islands of Greece. Wine has been produced there since ancient times, but it was during the Middle Ages that the wine of Santorini became famous worldwide under the influence of the Republic of Venice. The Italian influence is still present in modern Santorini winemaking: the most famous Tuscan sweet wine is called Vin Santo just like Santorini's Vinsanto/Visanto. It is made in a passito style from grapes dried in the sun after harvest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Asirtiko_Athiri_from_Santorini.JPG/330px-Asirtiko_Athiri_from_Santorini.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santorini_(wine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Santorini_Montage_L.png/500px-Santorini_Montage_L.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Santorini_Montage_L.png/500px-Santorini_Montage_L.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASantorini_Montage_L.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/500px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/1280px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/500px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Springtime landscape in a Fresco from the Bronze Age, Akrotiri","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg/330px-Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg/330px-Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"saffron-gatherers\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Stoa_Basilica.jpg/500px-Stoa_Basilica.jpg?utm_source=en.wi